</table>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In Fig. <a href="#S5.F5" title="Fig. 5 ‣ V-B2 Size-generalizability ‣ V-B Specific PE-Formers: Impact of Modules and Composition ‣ V Simulations ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> (see next page), we show the size-generalizability for MU-MIMO precoding. We can see that the specific PE-Former performs the best and is well-generalizable to different values of <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathsf{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗍</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathsf{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathsf{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗋</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathsf{r}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The 2D-Former is also size-generalizable but performs worse than the specific PE-Former, due to the approximation error. The Hier-Former is generalizable to the values of <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathsf{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗋</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathsf{r}}</annotation></semantics></math>, but cannot be generalized to the values of <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathsf{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗍</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathsf{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This is because the PE property induced by the <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{AN}^{\tt BS}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext>AN</mtext><mi>𝙱𝚂</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{AN}^{\tt BS}</annotation></semantics></math> set
is overlooked. The Edge-GCN can be generalized to different values of <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathsf{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗍</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathsf{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathsf{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗋</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathsf{r}}</annotation></semantics></math>, but does not perform well, again due to not using an attention mechanism.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S5.F5.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.08614v1/gen_N.svg" id="S5.F5.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:148/78;" width="148" height="78"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F5.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="S5.F5.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Generalizability to <math id="S5.F5.sf1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathsf{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗍</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathsf{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.F5.sf1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=4,N_{\mathsf{r},k}=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>𝗋</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=4,N_{\mathsf{r},k}=4</annotation></semantics></math></span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S5.F5.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.08614v1/gen_K.svg" id="S5.F5.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:148/78;" width="148" height="78"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F5.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="S5.F5.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Generalizability to <math id="S5.F5.sf2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.F5.sf2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathsf{t}}=64,N_{\mathsf{r},k}=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗍</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>𝗋</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathsf{t}}=64,N_{\mathsf{r},k}=4</annotation></semantics></math></span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S5.F5.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.08614v1/gen_r.svg" id="S5.F5.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:148/78;" width="148" height="78"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F5.sf3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(c)</span> </span><span id="S5.F5.sf3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Generalizability to <math id="S5.F5.sf3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathsf{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗋</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathsf{r}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.F5.sf3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathsf{t}}=64,K=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗍</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathsf{t}}=64,K=8</annotation></semantics></math></span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 5: </span>Size-generalizability for MU-MIMO precoding, SNR = 10 dB</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In Fig. <a href="#S5.F6" title="Fig. 6 ‣ V-B2 Size-generalizability ‣ V-B Specific PE-Formers: Impact of Modules and Composition ‣ V Simulations ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> (see next page), we show the size-generalizability for CB. Similarly, the results show that the specific PE-Former performs the best and is well-generalizable to different values of <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathsf{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗍</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathsf{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>. The 2D-Former is generalizable to different values of <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathsf{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗍</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathsf{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, but performs worse than the specific PE-Former. The Hier-Former cannot be generalized to the values of <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathsf{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗍</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathsf{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> due to the overlooked PE property induced by the <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{AN}^{\tt BS}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext>AN</mtext><mi>𝙱𝚂</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{AN}^{\tt BS}</annotation></semantics></math> set, whose size depends on the values of <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathsf{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗍</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathsf{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.SSS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>. The Edge-GCN is size-generalizable but performs the worst due to the lack of attention mechanism.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S5.F6.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.08614v1/gen_N_CB.svg" id="S5.F6.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:148/78;" width="148" height="78"></object>
