</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">VI </span><span id="S6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Conclusion</span></h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, we proposed a PE-MoFormer, a compositional DNN for learning a wide range of wireless problems with diverse PE properties. Specifically, we designed three modules that satisfy the nested 1D-PE, partial-nested 2D-PE, and joint 2D-PE properties, respectively. These modules, together with previously-designed modules, can be flexibly composed into 10 specific PE-Formers, each of which can be applied to the policies with one type of PE property. Building on the plug-and-play modules, we devised the PE-MoFormer that assembles two or three modules chosen from the seven modules by a selector, enabling a single model to learn over 25 wireless policies with 10 types of PE properties and without PE property. Simulation results showed that the PE-MoFormer performs well on multiple wireless tasks with low complexity, and exhibits strong generalizability across different problem scales, SNRs, and channel statistics.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This compositional design framework provides a foundation for extensions: new modules can be seamlessly inserted to accommodate more wireless problems with other PE properties when needed. Future work includes further reducing inference complexity and exploring the applicability of this framework to broader classes of wireless problems.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ IV-A2 Hypothesis Space of a DNN Consisting of Layers with Different PE Properties ‣ IV-A Hypothesis Spaces of DNNs ‣ IV Specific PE-Formers and PE-MoFormer ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Without loss of generality, consider <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\text{ind. 2D-PE}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mtext>ind. 2D-PE</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\text{ind. 2D-PE}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{1}\subsetneq\mathcal{F}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⊊</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{1}\subsetneq\mathcal{F}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. In other words, <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\Theta_{1}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\Theta_{1}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the ind. 2D-PE property, and <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\Theta_{2}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\Theta_{2}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies one type of the PE properties in (<a href="#S2.E1.1" title="In 1 ‣ II-A2 PE Properties ‣ II-A PE Properties of Functions Defined on Different Sets ‣ II PE Properties and Wireless Policies ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1a</span></a>), (<a href="#S2.E1.2" title="In II-A2 PE Properties ‣ II-A PE Properties of Functions Defined on Different Sets ‣ II PE Properties and Wireless Policies ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1b</span></a>) and (<a href="#S2.E2.2" title="In II-A2 PE Properties ‣ II-A PE Properties of Functions Defined on Different Sets ‣ II PE Properties and Wireless Policies ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2b</span></a>) - (<a href="#S2.E2.6" title="In II-A2 PE Properties ‣ II-A PE Properties of Functions Defined on Different Sets ‣ II PE Properties and Wireless Policies ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2f</span></a>). For notational simplicity, we omit the subscripts of <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\Theta_{2}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\Theta_{2}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\Theta_{1}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\Theta_{1}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the 1D-PE property in (<a href="#S2.E1.1" title="In 1 ‣ II-A2 PE Properties ‣ II-A PE Properties of Functions Defined on Different Sets ‣ II PE Properties and Wireless Policies ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1a</span></a>), then <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(g(\mathbf{X}\mathbf{\Pi}))\overset{(a)}{=}f(g(\mathbf{X})\mathbf{\Pi})\overset{(b)}{=}f(g(\mathbf{X}))\mathbf{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚷</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚷</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">b</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚷</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(g(\mathbf{X}\mathbf{\Pi}))\overset{(a)}{=}f(g(\mathbf{X})\mathbf{\Pi})\overset{(b)}{=}f(g(\mathbf{X}))\mathbf{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a)</annotation></semantics></math> holds because <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the ind. 2D-PE property in (<a href="#S2.E2.1" title="In II-A2 PE Properties ‣ II-A PE Properties of Functions Defined on Different Sets ‣ II PE Properties and Wireless Policies ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2a</span></a>) (thus also satisfies the 1D-PE property, see Fig. <a href="#S4.F2" title="Fig. 2 ‣ IV-A1 Hypothesis Spaces of DNNs with Different PE Properties ‣ IV-A Hypothesis Spaces of DNNs ‣ IV Specific PE-Formers and PE-MoFormer ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), and <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b)</annotation></semantics></math> holds because <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the 1D-PE property. Hence, <math id="A1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(g(\cdot))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(g(\cdot))</annotation></semantics></math> has the 1D-PE property. Since <math id="A1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{X}\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}})\neq\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}f(\mathbf{X})\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖡</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖡</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{X}\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}})\neq\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}f(\mathbf{X})\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(g(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{X}\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}))=f(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}g(\mathbf{X})\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}})\neq\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}f(g(\mathbf{X}))\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖡</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖡</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖡</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(g(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{X}\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}))=f(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}g(\mathbf{X})\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}})\neq\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}f(g(\mathbf{X}))\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, indicating that <math id="A1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(g(\cdot))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(g(\cdot))</annotation></semantics></math> does not satisfy the 2D-PE property.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the joint 2D-PE property in (<a href="#S2.E2.2" title="In II-A2 PE Properties ‣ II-A PE Properties of Functions Defined on Different Sets ‣ II PE Properties and Wireless Policies ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2b</span></a>), then
<math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}g(\mathbf{X})\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}})=\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}f(g(\mathbf{X}))\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖡</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖡</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}g(\mathbf{X})\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}})=\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}f(g(\mathbf{X}))\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> holds if and only if <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}=\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖠</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖡</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}=\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, when <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}=\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}=\mathbf{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖠</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖡</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝚷</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}=\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}=\mathbf{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(g(\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{X}\mathbf{\Pi}))\overset{(a)}{=}f(\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}g(\mathbf{X})\mathbf{\Pi})=\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}f(g(\mathbf{X}))\mathbf{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚷</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚷</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚷</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(g(\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{X}\mathbf{\Pi}))\overset{(a)}{=}f(\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}g(\mathbf{X})\mathbf{\Pi})=\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}f(g(\mathbf{X}))\mathbf{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a)</annotation></semantics></math> holds because <math id="A1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the ind. 2D-PE property. When <math id="A1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}\neq\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖠</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖡</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}\neq\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(g(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{X}\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}))=f(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}g(\mathbf{X})\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}})\neq\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}f(g(\mathbf{X}))\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖡</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖡</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖡</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(g(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{X}\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}))=f(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}g(\mathbf{X})\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}})\neq\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}f(g(\mathbf{X}))\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, <math id="A1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(g(\cdot))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(g(\cdot))</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the joint 2D-PE property but not the ind. 2D-PE property.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the partial-nested 2D-PE property in (<a href="#S2.E2.3" title="In II-A2 PE Properties ‣ II-A PE Properties of Functions Defined on Different Sets ‣ II PE Properties and Wireless Policies ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2c</span></a>), then
<math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}g(\mathbf{X})\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}})=\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}f(g(\mathbf{X}))\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖡</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖡</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}g(\mathbf{X})\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}})=\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}f(g(\mathbf{X}))\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> holds if and only if <math id="A1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}=\mathbf{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖡</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}=\mathbf{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, when <math id="A1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}=\mathbf{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖡</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}=\mathbf{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(g(\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}_{\mathsf{A}}\mathbf{X}\mathbf{\Omega}))=f(\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}_{\mathsf{A}}g(\mathbf{X})\mathbf{\Omega})=\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}_{\mathsf{A}}f(g(\mathbf{X}))\mathbf{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(g(\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}_{\mathsf{A}}\mathbf{X}\mathbf{\Omega}))=f(\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}_{\mathsf{A}}g(\mathbf{X})\mathbf{\Omega})=\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}_{\mathsf{A}}f(g(\mathbf{X}))\mathbf{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="A1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}\neq\mathbf{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖡</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}\neq\mathbf{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math> , <math id="A1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(g(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{X}\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}))\neq\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}f(g(\mathbf{X}))\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖡</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖠</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖡</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(g(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{X}\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}))\neq\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{A}}^{\mathsf{T}}f(g(\mathbf{X}))\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, <math id="A1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(g(\cdot))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(g(\cdot))</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the partial-nested 2D-PE property but not ind. 2D-PE property.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the PE properties in (<a href="#S2.E1.2" title="In II-A2 PE Properties ‣ II-A PE Properties of Functions Defined on Different Sets ‣ II PE Properties and Wireless Policies ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1b</span></a>), (<a href="#S2.E2.4" title="In II-A2 PE Properties ‣ II-A PE Properties of Functions Defined on Different Sets ‣ II PE Properties and Wireless Policies ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2d</span></a>)-(<a href="#S2.E2.6" title="In II-A2 PE Properties ‣ II-A PE Properties of Functions Defined on Different Sets ‣ II PE Properties and Wireless Policies ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2f</span></a>), we can also prove that <math id="A1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(g(\cdot))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(g(\cdot))</annotation></semantics></math> has the same PE property as <math id="A1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> but not the ind. 2D-PE property, using similar derivations.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2. ‣ IV-B1 Nested Attention Sub-layers ‣ IV-B Design of Three Modules ‣ IV Specific PE-Formers and PE-MoFormer ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first define a mask matrix <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐌</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows,</p>
<table id="A2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}\triangleq\mathbf{I}_{\mathsf{sub}}\otimes\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}}=\mathrm{diag}(\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}},\cdots,\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>≜</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}\triangleq\mathbf{I}_{\mathsf{sub}}\otimes\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}}=\mathrm{diag}(\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}},\cdots,\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}}</annotation></semantics></math> represents a <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathsf{s}}\times N_{\mathsf{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathsf{s}}\times N_{\mathsf{s}}</annotation></semantics></math> all-one matrix.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">It is not hard to prove that</p>
<table id="A2.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Pi}\mathbf{M}\neq\mathbf{M}\mathbf{\Pi}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚷</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚷</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Pi}\mathbf{M}\neq\mathbf{M}\mathbf{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any nested permutation matrix <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Omega}=(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}}\otimes\mathbf{I}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})\mathrm{diag}(\mathbf{\Pi}_{1},\cdots,\mathbf{\Pi}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝛀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Omega}=(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}}\otimes\mathbf{I}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})\mathrm{diag}(\mathbf{\Pi}_{1},\cdots,\mathbf{\Pi}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}\mathbf{\Omega}=\mathbf{\Omega}\mathbf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝛀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}\mathbf{\Omega}=\mathbf{\Omega}\mathbf{M}</annotation></semantics></math> holds.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first prove the following equality,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}}\otimes\mathbf{I}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})=(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}}\otimes\mathbf{I}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})\mathbf{M}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}}\otimes\mathbf{I}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})=(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}}\otimes\mathbf{I}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})\mathbf{M}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The left-hand side of (<a href="#A2.E3" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Proposition ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>) can be re-written as <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}}\otimes\mathbf{I}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})=(\mathbf{I}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}}\otimes\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}})\cdot(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}}\otimes\mathbf{I}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})\overset{(a)}{=}(\mathbf{I}_{\mathsf{sub}}\cdot\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}})\otimes(\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}}\cdot\mathbf{I}_{\mathsf{sub}})=\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}}\otimes\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}}\otimes\mathbf{I}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})=(\mathbf{I}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}}\otimes\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}})\cdot(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}}\otimes\mathbf{I}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})\overset{(a)}{=}(\mathbf{I}_{\mathsf{sub}}\cdot\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}})\otimes(\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}}\cdot\mathbf{I}_{\mathsf{sub}})=\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}}\otimes\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a)</annotation></semantics></math> is due to <math id="A2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{A}\otimes\mathbf{B})\cdot(\mathbf{C}\otimes\mathbf{D})=(\mathbf{A}\cdot\mathbf{C})\otimes(\mathbf{B}\cdot\mathbf{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝐁</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐂</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝐃</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐂</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐃</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{A}\otimes\mathbf{B})\cdot(\mathbf{C}\otimes\mathbf{D})=(\mathbf{A}\cdot\mathbf{C})\otimes(\mathbf{B}\cdot\mathbf{D})</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, the right-hand side can be re-written as <math id="A2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}}\otimes\mathbf{I}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})\mathbf{M}=(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}}\otimes\mathbf{I}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})\cdot(\mathbf{I}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}}\otimes\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}})=(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}}\cdot\mathbf{I}_{\mathsf{sub}})\otimes(\mathbf{I}_{\mathsf{sub}}\cdot\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}})=\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}}\otimes\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}}\otimes\mathbf{I}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})\mathbf{M}=(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}}\otimes\mathbf{I}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})\cdot(\mathbf{I}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}}\otimes\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}})=(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}}\cdot\mathbf{I}_{\mathsf{sub}})\otimes(\mathbf{I}_{\mathsf{sub}}\cdot\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}})=\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}}\otimes\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which equals the left-hand side.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is an all-one matrix, <math id="A2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}}\mathbf{\Pi}=\mathbf{\Pi}\,\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚷</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝚷</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}}\mathbf{\Pi}=\mathbf{\Pi}\,\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}}</annotation></semantics></math> for any permutation matrix <math id="A2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚷</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E4X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E4X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{M}\cdot\mathrm{diag}(\mathbf{\Pi}_{1},\cdots,\mathbf{\Pi}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})=\mathrm{diag}(\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}}\mathbf{\Pi}_{1},\cdots,\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}}\mathbf{\Pi}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{M}\cdot\mathrm{diag}(\mathbf{\Pi}_{1},\cdots,\mathbf{\Pi}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})=\mathrm{diag}(\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}}\mathbf{\Pi}_{1},\cdots,\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}}\mathbf{\Pi}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(B.4)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E4Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E4Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{diag}(\mathbf{\Pi}_{1}\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}},\cdots,\mathbf{\Pi}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}}\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}})=\mathrm{diag}(\mathbf{\Pi}_{1},\cdots,\mathbf{\Pi}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})\mathbf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{diag}(\mathbf{\Pi}_{1}\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}},\cdots,\mathbf{\Pi}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}}\mathbf{1}_{N_{\mathsf{s}}})=\mathrm{diag}(\mathbf{\Pi}_{1},\cdots,\mathbf{\Pi}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})\mathbf{M}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, we can derive that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex1X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex1X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{M\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{M\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex1X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{M}(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}}\otimes\mathbf{I}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})\mathrm{diag}(\mathbf{\Pi}_{1},\cdots,\mathbf{\Pi}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{M}(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}}\otimes\mathbf{I}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})\mathrm{diag}(\mathbf{\Pi}_{1},\cdots,\mathbf{\Pi}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex1Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex1Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{=}(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}}\otimes\mathbf{I}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})\mathbf{M}\mathrm{diag}(\mathbf{\Pi}_{1},\cdots,\mathbf{\Pi}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐌</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{=}(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}}\otimes\mathbf{I}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})\mathbf{M}\mathrm{diag}(\mathbf{\Pi}_{1},\cdots,\mathbf{\Pi}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex1Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex1Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{=}(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}}\otimes\mathbf{I}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})\mathrm{diag}(\mathbf{\Pi}_{1},\cdots,\mathbf{\Pi}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})\mathbf{M}=\mathbf{\Omega M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">b</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝛀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{=}(\mathbf{\Pi}_{\mathsf{sub}}\otimes\mathbf{I}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})\mathrm{diag}(\mathbf{\Pi}_{1},\cdots,\mathbf{\Pi}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}}})\mathbf{M}=\mathbf{\Omega M}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b)</annotation></semantics></math> come from (<a href="#A2.E3" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Proposition ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>) and (<a href="#A2.E4" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Proposition ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>), respectively.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p7.2" class="ltx_p">Denote <math id="A2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{C}^{(\ell)}=[\mathbf{c}_{1_{1}}^{(\ell)},\cdots,\mathbf{c}_{1_{N_{\mathsf{s}}}}^{(\ell)},\cdots,\mathbf{c}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}{N_{\mathsf{s}}}}}^{(\ell)}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐜</mi><msub><mn>1</mn><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐜</mi><msub><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐜</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{C}^{(\ell)}=[\mathbf{c}_{1_{1}}^{(\ell)},\cdots,\mathbf{c}_{1_{N_{\mathsf{s}}}}^{(\ell)},\cdots,\mathbf{c}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}{N_{\mathsf{s}}}}}^{(\ell)}]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{D}^{(\ell)}=[\mathbf{d}_{1_{1}}^{(\ell)},\cdots,\mathbf{d}_{1_{N_{\mathsf{s}}}}^{(\ell)},\cdots,\mathbf{d}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}{N_{\mathsf{s}}}}}^{(\ell)}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐝</mi><msub><mn>1</mn><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐝</mi><msub><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐝</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>𝗌𝗎𝖻</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>𝗌</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{D}^{(\ell)}=[\mathbf{d}_{1_{1}}^{(\ell)},\cdots,\mathbf{d}_{1_{N_{\mathsf{s}}}}^{(\ell)},\cdots,\mathbf{d}_{N_{\mathsf{sub}{N_{\mathsf{s}}}}}^{(\ell)}]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{D}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{D}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math> as the input and output representations of all tokens in NATT. The input-output relation of NATT in (<a href="#S4.E9" title="In IV-B1 Nested Attention Sub-layers ‣ IV-B Design of Three Modules ‣ IV Specific PE-Formers and PE-MoFormer ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) can be expressed in matrix form as,</p>
<table id="A2.E5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E5X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E5X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{C}^{(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{C}^{(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E5X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{V}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\Big(\big(\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{K}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\big)^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D^{(\ell-1)}}\odot\mathbf{M}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝖲</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝖲</mi><mi>𝖪</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{V}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\Big(\big(\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{K}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\big)^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D^{(\ell-1)}}\odot\mathbf{M}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(B.5)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E5Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E5Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{D}}^{\mathsf{V}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\big(\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{D}}^{\mathsf{K}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\big)^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D^{(\ell-1)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝖣</mi><mi>𝖪</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{D}}^{\mathsf{V}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\big(\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{D}}^{\mathsf{K}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\big)^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D^{(\ell-1)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E5Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E5Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\triangleq F(\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)})+G(\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\triangleq F(\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)})+G(\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p7.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> respectively represent the local attention and global attention mechanism, where <math id="A2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the 1D-PE property as proved in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we prove that <math id="A2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is with the nested 1D-PE property, i.e., <math id="A2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega})=F(\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)})\mathbf{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega})=F(\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)})\mathbf{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p9.2" class="ltx_p">According to the definition of <math id="A2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A2.E5" title="In Appendix B Proof of Proposition ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>), we have,</p>
<table id="A2.E6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E6X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E6X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F(\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega})\!=\!\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{V}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\Big(\big(\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{K}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\big)^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D^{(\ell-1)}}\mathbf{\Omega}\!\odot\!\mathbf{M}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝖲</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝖲</mi><mi>𝖪</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F(\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega})\!=\!\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{V}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\Big(\big(\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{K}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\big)^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D^{(\ell-1)}}\mathbf{\Omega}\!\odot\!\mathbf{M}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(B.6)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E6Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E6Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{V}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\Big(\mathbf{\Omega}^{\mathsf{T}}\big(\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{K}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\big)^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\!\odot\!\mathbf{M}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝖲</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝖲</mi><mi>𝖪</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{V}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\Big(\mathbf{\Omega}^{\mathsf{T}}\big(\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{K}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\big)^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\!\odot\!\mathbf{M}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">For any permutation matrices <math id="A2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Pi}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Pi}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Pi}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Pi}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, it is not hard to prove that</p>
<table id="A2.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Pi}_{1}(\mathbf{A}\odot\mathbf{B})\mathbf{\Pi}_{2}=(\mathbf{\Pi}_{1}\mathbf{A}\mathbf{\Pi}_{2})\odot(\mathbf{\Pi}_{1}\mathbf{B}\mathbf{\Pi}_{2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Pi}_{1}(\mathbf{A}\odot\mathbf{B})\mathbf{\Pi}_{2}=(\mathbf{\Pi}_{1}\mathbf{A}\mathbf{\Pi}_{2})\odot(\mathbf{\Pi}_{1}\mathbf{B}\mathbf{\Pi}_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p11.2" class="ltx_p">By using (<a href="#A2.E7" title="In Appendix B Proof of Proposition ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.7</span></a>) and Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Proposition ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, (<a href="#A2.E6" title="In Appendix B Proof of Proposition ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a>) can be re-written as,</p>
<table id="A2.E8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E8X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E8X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{V}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\Big(\mathbf{\Omega}^{\mathsf{T}}\big(\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{K}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\big)^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\!\odot\!\mathbf{M}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝖲</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝖲</mi><mi>𝖪</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{V}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\Big(\mathbf{\Omega}^{\mathsf{T}}\big(\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{K}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\big)^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\!\odot\!\mathbf{M}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="5" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(B.8)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E8Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E8Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{=}\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{V}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\Big(\big(\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{K}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\big)^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\odot\mathbf{\Omega}\mathbf{M}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝖲</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝖲</mi><mi>𝖪</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{=}\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{V}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\Big(\big(\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{K}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\big)^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\odot\mathbf{\Omega}\mathbf{M}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E8Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E8Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{=}\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{V}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\Big(\big(\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{K}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\big)^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\odot\mathbf{M}\mathbf{\Omega}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">b</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝖲</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝖲</mi><mi>𝖪</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{=}\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{V}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\Big(\big(\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{K}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\big)^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\odot\mathbf{M}\mathbf{\Omega}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E8Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E8Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(c)}{=}\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{V}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\Big(\big(\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{K}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\big)^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\odot\mathbf{M}\Big)\mathbf{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">c</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝖲</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝖲</mi><mi>𝖪</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(c)}{=}\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{V}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\Big(\big(\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{K}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\big)^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\odot\mathbf{M}\Big)\mathbf{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E8Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E8Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(d)}{=}F(\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)})\mathbf{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">d</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(d)}{=}F(\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)})\mathbf{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p11.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a)</annotation></semantics></math> comes from (<a href="#A2.E7" title="In Appendix B Proof of Proposition ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.7</span></a>) by letting <math id="A2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Pi}_{1}=\mathbf{\Omega},\mathbf{\Pi}_{2}=\mathbf{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Pi}_{1}=\mathbf{\Omega},\mathbf{\Pi}_{2}=\mathbf{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b)</annotation></semantics></math> is due to Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Proposition ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <math id="A2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(c)</annotation></semantics></math> comes from (<a href="#A2.E7" title="In Appendix B Proof of Proposition ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.7</span></a>) by letting <math id="A2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Pi}_{1}=\mathbf{I},\mathbf{\Pi}_{2}=\mathbf{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚷</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Pi}_{1}=\mathbf{I},\mathbf{\Pi}_{2}=\mathbf{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d)</annotation></semantics></math> is due to the definition of <math id="A2.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p12.1" class="ltx_p">From (<a href="#A2.E6" title="In Appendix B Proof of Proposition ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a>) and (<a href="#A2.E8" title="In Appendix B Proof of Proposition ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.8</span></a>), we have <math id="A2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega})=F(\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)})\mathbf{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega})=F(\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)})\mathbf{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the nested 1D-PE property.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p13.1" class="ltx_p">When the nested permutation matrix <math id="A2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝛀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math> is replaced by arbitrary permutation matrix <math id="A2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚷</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Pi})\neq F(\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)})\mathbf{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚷</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚷</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Pi})\neq F(\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)})\mathbf{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math> due to (<a href="#A2.E2" title="In Appendix B Proof of Proposition ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>), i.e., <math id="A2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> does not satisfy the 1D-PE property.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p14.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> respectively satisfy the nested 1D-PE and 1D-PE property, it can be proved that the input-output relation of the NATT, i.e., <math id="A2.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\cdot)+G(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\cdot)+G(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, satisfies the nested 1D-PE property, using similar derivations in Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Proof of Proposition ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition3" title="Proposition 3. ‣ IV-B1 Nested Attention Sub-layers ‣ IV-B Design of Three Modules ‣ IV Specific PE-Formers and PE-MoFormer ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">With the four conditions in the proposition, it has been proved in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite> that <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A2.E5" title="In Appendix B Proof of Proposition ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>) satisfies the ind. 2D-PE property.
From the definition of <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A2.E5" title="In Appendix B Proof of Proposition ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>), we have,</p>
<table id="A3.E1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E1X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E1X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F(\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D^{(\ell-1)}}\mathbf{\Omega})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F(\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D^{(\ell-1)}}\mathbf{\Omega})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(C.1)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E1Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E1Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{V}}\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\Big(\big(\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{K}}\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\big)^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D^{(\ell-1)}}\mathbf{\Omega}\odot\mathbf{M}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝖲</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝖲</mi><mi>𝖪</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{V}}\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\Big(\big(\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{K}}\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\big)^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D^{(\ell-1)}}\mathbf{\Omega}\odot\mathbf{M}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Further using the given conditions <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Pi}\mathbf{U}^{\mathsf{K}}_{\mathsf{S}}=\mathbf{U}^{\mathsf{K}}_{\mathsf{S}}\mathbf{\Pi},\mathbf{\Pi}\mathbf{U}^{\mathsf{V}}_{\mathsf{S}}=\mathbf{U}^{\mathsf{V}}_{\mathsf{S}}\mathbf{\Pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚷</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝖲</mi><mi>𝖪</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝖲</mi><mi>𝖪</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚷</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚷</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝖲</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝖲</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚷</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Pi}\mathbf{U}^{\mathsf{K}}_{\mathsf{S}}=\mathbf{U}^{\mathsf{K}}_{\mathsf{S}}\mathbf{\Pi},\mathbf{\Pi}\mathbf{U}^{\mathsf{V}}_{\mathsf{S}}=\mathbf{U}^{\mathsf{V}}_{\mathsf{S}}\mathbf{\Pi}</annotation></semantics></math>, (<a href="#A3.E1" title="In Appendix C Proof of Proposition ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>) can be re-written as,</p>
<table id="A3.E2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E2X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E2X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{V}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\Big(\big(\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{K}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\big)^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\odot\mathbf{M}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝖲</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝖲</mi><mi>𝖪</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{V}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\Big(\big(\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{K}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\big)^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\odot\mathbf{M}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(C.2)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E2Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E2Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{=}\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{V}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\Big(\mathbf{\Omega}^{\mathsf{T}}\big(\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{K}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\big)^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\odot\mathbf{M}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝖲</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝛀</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐔</mi><mi>𝖲</mi><mi>𝖪</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>𝐌</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{=}\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{V}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\Big(\mathbf{\Omega}^{\mathsf{T}}\big(\mathbf{U}_{\mathsf{S}}^{\mathsf{K}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\big)^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega}\odot\mathbf{M}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E2Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E2Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{=}\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}F(\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)})\mathbf{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">b</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{=}\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}F(\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)})\mathbf{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a)</annotation></semantics></math> is due to <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Pi}\cdot\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}=\mathbf{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚷</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Pi}\cdot\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}=\mathbf{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b)</annotation></semantics></math> is due to (<a href="#A2.E8" title="In Appendix B Proof of Proposition ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.8</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">With (<a href="#A3.E1" title="In Appendix C Proof of Proposition ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>) and (<a href="#A3.E2" title="In Appendix C Proof of Proposition ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>), we have <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega})=\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}F(\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)})\mathbf{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚷</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐃</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)}\mathbf{\Omega})=\mathbf{\Pi}^{\mathsf{T}}F(\mathbf{D}^{(\ell-1)})\mathbf{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the parial-nested 2D-PE property in (<a href="#S2.E2.3" title="In II-A2 PE Properties ‣ II-A PE Properties of Functions Defined on Different Sets ‣ II PE Properties and Wireless Policies ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2c</span></a>). Since <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the ind. 2D-PE property, it can be proved that the input-output relation of NATT (P.S.), i.e., <math id="A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\cdot)+G(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\cdot)+G(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, satisfies the partial-nested 2D-PE property, using similar derivations in Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Proof of Proposition ‣ Modular PE-Structured Learning for Cross-Task Wireless Communications" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="bib" class="ltx_bibliography">
